.TH "HTMLVIDEOELEMENT.DISABLEPICTUREINPICTURE" "3JS" "August 21, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLVideoElement.disablePictureInPicture \- HTMLVideoElement:
disablePictureInPicture property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]disablePictureInPicture\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]HTMLVideoElement\f[R] interface reflects the
\f[CR]disablepictureinpicture\f[R] HTML attribute indicating whether the
picture\-in\-picture feature is disabled for the current element.
.PP
This value only represents a request from the website to the user agent.
User configuration may change the eventual behavior\(emfor example,
Firefox users can change the
\f[CR]media.videocontrols.picture\-in\-picture.respect\-disablePictureInPicture\f[R]
setting to ignore the request to disable PiP.
.SH VALUE
A boolean value that is \f[CR]true\f[R] if the picture\-in\-picture
feature is disabled for this element.
.PP
When \f[CR]true\f[R], the user agent will not suggest
picture\-in\-picture to users, or request it automatically.
